From: gaokun-Android project
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3: drive touch mode
 select gpio174 low

The HX83121A cascade TDDI IC selects its host transport at touch
firmware reload time by sampling gpio174:

  - gpio174 LOW  at reload -> SPI raw-data mode (himax-spi driver)
  - gpio174 HIGH at reload -> I2C HID mode (used by UEFI/BIOS)

Reference: refs/linux-gaokun/README.MD "Touchscreen / insights":
  "In practical, we should set gpio174 before firmware reload (reload
   will auto trigger internally after TS reset(gpio99), display reset
   (gpio38) may trigger TS reset internally). After that, set gpio174
   to any state is safe."

Neither the buildbot DTS nor the linux-gaokun DTS configures gpio174,
so the pin floats at whatever level UEFI left it. UEFI itself uses the
I2C HID mode (BIOS touch), so boots frequently latch the IC into I2C
mode, leaving the SPI driver probing successfully ("FW reload done")
but completely deaf: zero real-touch events, spurious ghost frames.
Any display reset (e.g. a KMS mode switch) can silently re-trigger a
fw reload and flip the latched mode, which makes the failure appear
and disappear across reboots "randomly".

Fix: pin gpio174 permanently low via the touchscreen pinctrl default
state. Applied at himax-spi probe, i.e. before the driver-initiated
TS reset -> fw reload, and held low across all later panel-follower
reinits. output-low usage pattern verified against jhovold
sc8280xp-crd.dts:975-978 (same SoC, same tlmm driver).

Verified 2026-08-17 on GK-W7X (BIOS 2.16, touch fw 41 07):
  - Ubuntu 7.1.0-rc3 + gpioset 174=0 + driver rebind: touch tracks
    perfectly (user: "非常跟手")
  - Android 16 + this DTB change: touch smooth end to end
    (user: "触摸非常丝滑"); idle IRQ streams at display scan rate
    (~120/s @ 120Hz panel, ~60/s @ 60Hz) which is normal for the raw
    tx-rx reporting mode.

Apply to: arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
(kernel tree on build VM: ~/gaokun/mainline-linux)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
@@ -1658,6 +1658,12 @@
 	};

 	ts0_default: ts0-default-state {
+		mode-pins {
+			pins = "gpio174";
+			function = "gpio";
+			output-low;
+		};
+
 		int-n-pins {
 			pins = "gpio175";
 			function = "gpio";
